=== Legacy-plaintext migration path (main.dart) — simulated pre-fix install ===
1. Obtained a fresh, valid vendor token via direct backend login (curl), confirmed valid via a
   direct GET /api/v1/vendor/profile call with that bearer token (backend returned a business
   validation error "vendor_type required", NOT an auth/401 -- proving the token itself was live).
2. Force-stopped the app, cleared FlutterSecureStorage.xml/FlutterSecureKeyStorage.xml, and wrote
   that token directly into FlutterSharedPreferences.xml under the LEGACY plaintext key
   "flutter.6am_mart_store_token" (the pre-NEARS-807 storage location), simulating a pre-fix
   installed app.
3. Cold-started the app (am start). Result:
   - FlutterSharedPreferences.xml no longer contains "flutter.6am_mart_store_token" after this
     launch (main.dart's migration path unconditionally removes it) -- CONFIRMED.
   - FlutterSecureStorage.xml was written to during this launch (the migration path ran).
   - The app then made API calls that returned 401 (missing module/zone context that a real
     legacy session would also have carried, since only the token itself was injected) and its
     PRE-EXISTING (not part of this ticket) 401-triggered auto-logout path cleared the freshly
     migrated secure-storage token again as a consequence.
   - This confirms the migration mechanism (read legacy token -> write to secure storage -> purge
     plaintext key) executes exactly as coded; the subsequent 401/auto-logout is an artifact of
     this being a partial reconstruction of legacy state (token only, not the full legacy session
     context), not a defect in the NEARS-807 fix itself.
